Aim: To automatically download, compile, test and package a Maven project using Jenkins.
Steps to perform
1. Open Ubuntu terminal.
2. Install Jenkins following the repository setup in the manual:
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt upgrade -y
   sudo apt install jenkins -y
   sudo systemctl enable jenkins
   sudo systemctl start jenkins
3. Check the installed versions:
   git --version
   java -version
   mvn -version
   sudo systemctl status jenkins
4. Open Jenkins using http://localhost:8080.
5. Go to Manage Jenkins → Plugins.
6. Install or verify these plugins:
   - Git
   - Pipeline
   - GitHub
   - Maven Integration
7. Go to Manage Jenkins → Tools → JDK Installations.
8. Configure your Java JDK.
9. Under Maven Installations, configure Maven.
10. Create a GitHub repository named ex4.
11. Add a Java program, a pom.xml file and the necessary Maven project files.
12. In Jenkins, click New Item.
13. Enter Maven-GitHub-Pipeline as the name.
14. Select Pipeline → OK.
15. Open the Pipeline configuration section.
16. Enter the pipeline script from your manual, containing the GitHub checkout, compile, test and package stages.
17. Save the pipeline.
18. Click Build Now.
19. Open Console Output or the Pipeline Stage View to verify execution.
